<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine bonds not traded due to Thanksgiving.</title>
<headline>Argentine bonds not traded due to Thanksgiving.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine bonds were unquoted Thursday as the market stood at a standstill because of the closure of the U.S. markets for Thanksgiving.</p>
<p>Not a single trade was recorded on screens.</p>
<p>The dollar-denominated Bocon Previsional 2 due 2001 closed Wednesday at 121.10, while Argentina's FRB due 2005 was flat at  85-6/8.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
